alse,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.027520083749375757,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":29.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04623346243055804,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":62.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.020517545563633943,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":75.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.015650803786143964,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":73.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.12211,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":81.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Victory Capital Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an asset management company in the United States and internationally. It offers specialized investment strategies to institutions, intermediaries, retirement platforms, and individual investors. The company also provides various investment products, including actively and passively managed mutual funds, rules-based and active exchange traded funds (ETF), institutional separate accounts, variable insurance products, alternative investments, private closed end funds, and a 529 education savings plan; and third-party investment products, such as mutual funds, third-party ETF model strategies, retail separately managed accounts, unified managed accounts, collective investment trusts, undertakings for the collective investment in transferable securities, and other pooled vehicles. In addition, it offers investment management services, fund administration services, fund transfer agent services, and fund distribution services. The company has a strategic collaboration with Apollo Global Management, Inc. to expand private markets access to a range of investors through diversified investment solutions. Victory Capital Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2013 and is based in San Antonio, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David Craig Brown CPA | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 52 | Compensation: $6.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 699 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $546K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $29K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Victory Capital Holdings, Inc.  is a mid-cap financial services business with a $7.6B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $381M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 19% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.18888373828433574},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Victory Capital Holdings (VCTR) Rose on Record Q2 Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/victory-capital-holdings-vctr-rose-164657364.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795711617.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (VCTR) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_VCTR_That_Institutions_Follow_112426020802_1795504082.html","date":"